And they, as a great wave of the wide-wayed sea
over a ship’s sides comes down, whenever presses it hard
the force of the wind; for that it is that most of all increases waves;

but the Achaeans
the Trojans coming on awaited steadily, nor were able,
though fewer they were, to push them off from the ships;

“Teucer, good one, now for us two has been killed our trusty companion,
Mastor’s-son, whom we two, from Cythera, when he was within,
equally with dear parents honoured in the halls;

So he spoke, and he understood, and running, close beside him stood,
holding in his hand the back-stretched bow and the quiver,
arrow-receiving;

And he struck Cleitus, Peisenor’s splendid son,
companion of noble Polydamas, Panthous’-son,
holding the reins in his hands;

These he to Astynous, the son of Protiaon, gave,
and much urged him close at hand to hold,
watching, the horses;
